From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c0de-coffee <53132135+c0de-coffee@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:15:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] rdp-pipewire-stream: Tell the compositor where each virtual
 monitor is

The compositor creates one virtual monitor per client monitor, but only
learns their sizes and scales. It doesn't know how the client arranges
them or which one is primary, so it lays them out in creation order (the
client's monitor order), which may not match the client: moving a window
to the monitor on the left can move it to the one on the right, and
windows open on whichever monitor came first rather than the primary one.

Add the monitor's position in the client's layout (physical pixels,
primary monitor at 0,0) and whether it's the primary monitor to the tag
that already carries the preferred scale. Compositors that don't know
these keys ignore them.
---
 src/grd-rdp-pipewire-stream.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/grd-rdp-pipewire-stream.c b/src/grd-rdp-pipewire-stream.c
index eae08d0..866eab6 100644
--- a/src/grd-rdp-pipewire-stream.c
+++ b/src/grd-rdp-pipewire-stream.c
@@ -380,8 +380,10 @@ add_tag_params (GrdRdpPipeWireStream        *stream,
                 GArray                      *pod_offsets)
 {
   struct spa_pod_frame tag_frame;
-  struct spa_dict_item items[1];
+  struct spa_dict_item items[4];
   char scale_string[G_ASCII_DTOSTR_BUF_SIZE];
+  char x_string[16];
+  char y_string[16];
   double scale;
 
   grd_append_pod_offset (pod_offsets, pod_builder);
@@ -393,6 +395,18 @@ add_tag_params (GrdRdpPipeWireStream        *stream,
   g_ascii_dtostr (scale_string, G_ASCII_DTOSTR_BUF_SIZE, scale);
   items[0] = SPA_DICT_ITEM_INIT ("org.gnome.preferred-scale", scale_string);
 
+  /*
+   * Where the monitor is in the client's monitor layout (physical pixels,
+   * primary monitor at 0,0), so that the compositor can arrange its virtual
+   * monitors the same way and put things on the primary one.
+   */
+  g_snprintf (x_string, sizeof (x_string), "%d", virtual_monitor->pos_x);
+  g_snprintf (y_string, sizeof (y_string), "%d", virtual_monitor->pos_y);
+  items[1] = SPA_DICT_ITEM_INIT ("org.gnome.position-x", x_string);
+  items[2] = SPA_DICT_ITEM_INIT ("org.gnome.position-y", y_string);
+  items[3] = SPA_DICT_ITEM_INIT ("org.gnome.is-primary",
+                                 virtual_monitor->is_primary ? "true" : "false");
+
   spa_tag_build_add_dict (pod_builder,
                           &SPA_DICT_INIT (items, G_N_ELEMENTS (items)));
 
